&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Vision Chain at the infrastructure level, managing configuration choices (fee mechanism, block building logic, etc.), and modifications to the OP Stack, in collaboration with the OP Labs team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage infrastructure partnerships, owning the technical relationship with providers (RPC nodes, indexing, oracles, etc.).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Compliance and Legal to implement regulatorily-compliant onchain transaction screening, identity, and privacy solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run reliability, incidents and cost, and own developer documentation and partner technical onboarding until a developer relations lead joins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the other Vision Web3 product leads to ensure the chain’s technical roadmap supports the product roadmap being built on top of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product or engineering experience, with 3+ years focused on blockchain infrastructure (e.g., L1/L2, rollup-as-a-service, node infrastructure provider, account abstraction, or an exchange protocol team).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of EVM rollup mechanics, including sequencing, fees, proofs, withdrawals, bridges, upgrade keys, and account abstraction.&lt;/li&gt;
